================================================================================
Modifications
================================================================================

Apache License 2.0, section 4(b): this section records which files differ from the
upstream model and how. All but the Unicode table derive from the model release:
the first is distributed byte-identical to the quantised artifact it comes from,
and the others are re-encoded or reimplemented here.

src/weights/qwen3.5-0.8b-q4.qwqt
    The model's weights in 4-bit groups with f16 scales, in the QWQT container
    format. The bytes are identical to the quantised artifact this
    build takes them from -- 494,845,446 bytes, SHA256
    29773850a7ac53122e1544a24748701b55fa59ca63fed89cae71b9baabc7dfb9, the same
    digest the input file has -- so this repository redistributes that artifact
    rather than quantising anything. The artifact is in turn a lossy 4-bit
    derivation of the release's bf16 safetensors (1,746,942,600 bytes), made
    outside this repository; its generator is not part of this repository.

src/tokenizer/data/tokenizer.bin
    The vocabulary, the merge table and the added tokens, re-encoded from
    tokenizer.json and tokenizer_config.json into a packed table: a byte table,
    merges sorted by pair, and offset-indexed token strings. The token strings
    and the merge pairs are the upstream ones; the layout and the indices are
    not.

src/tokenizer/data/unicode.bin
    Character classes, combining classes and normalisation tables, derived from
    the Unicode Character Database and from the observed behaviour of the
    reference tokenizer. See the Unicode notice below.

src/chat.rs
    The conversation template, reimplemented in Rust from chat_template.jinja.
    The template text itself is not copied into this repository.


